NAInt8MatMul register fragment implementation derived from MLX Steel

Upstream revision: 25532871329fe4cafdada9fa0941a1cdbfb3a9f2
Repository: https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx
Source: mlx/backend/metal/kernels/steel/gemm/gemm_nax.h
License: MIT (see LICENSE).

NAInt8MatMulKernel.cpp adapts Steel's 16x16 fragment coordinates, contiguous
loads, and M16/N32/K16 cooperative-tensor assembly. Each SIMD group computes
32x32 with INT8 operands and INT32 accumulators. Eight SIMD groups cover a
64x128 output tile; K advances by 32, with threadgroup synchronization every
512 and pairs of K32 steps exposed to the compiler. Partial output tiles mask
rows; the final short K step additionally masks reduction coordinates.

The generator implements this traversal directly, using NAInt8MatMul's buffer
bindings, shape function constants, runtime M, typed row scales, bias and output.
It does not import Steel's GEMM entry point, parameter ABI, generic traversal,
function constants, or textually rewrite external shader source.
